w: 1.~O Lord, thy judg- ments give the king, his son thy right- eous- ness. With right he shall thy peo- _ ple judge, thy poor with u- prigh- tness.
w: 2.~The lof- ty moun- tains shall bring forth un- to the peo- ple peace; Li- kewise the lit- tle hills _ the same shall do by right- eous- ness.
w: 3.~The peo- ple's poor ones he shall judge, the nee- dy's child- ren save; And those shall he in piec- _ es break who them op- press- èd have.
w: 4.~They shall thee fear, while sun and moon do last, through a- ges all. Like rain on mown grass he _ shall drop, or show'rs on earth that fall.
w: 5.~The just shall flour- ish in his days, and pros- per in his reign: He shall, while doth the moon _ en- dure, a- bun- dant peace main- tain.
w: 6.~His large and great do- min- ion shall from sea to sea ex- tend: It from the ri- ver shall _ reach forth un- to earth's ut- most end.
w: 7.~They in the wild- er- ness that dwell bow down be- fore him must; And they that are his e- _ ne- mies shall lick the ver- y dust.
w: 8.~The kings of Tar- shish, and the isles, to him shall pre- sents bring; And un- to him shall of- _ fer gifts She- ba's and Se- ba's king.
w: 9.~Yea, all the might- y kings on earth be- fore him down shall fall; And all the na- tions of _ the world do ser- vice to him shall.
w: 10.~For he the need- y shall pre- serve, when he to him doth call; The poor al- so, and him _ that hath no help of man at all.
w: 11.~The poor man and the in- di- gent in mer- cy he shall spare; He shall pre- serve a- live _ the souls of those that need- y are.
w: 12.~Both from de- ceit and vi- o- lence their soul he shall set free; And in his sight right pre- _ ci- ous and dear their blood shall be.
w: 13.~Yea, he shall live, and giv'n to him shall be of She- ba's gold: For him still shall they pray, _ and he shall dai- ly be ex- tolled.
w: 14.~Of corn an hand- ful in the earth on tops of moun- tains high, With pros- p'rous fruit shall shake, _ like trees on Le- ba- non that be.
w: 15.~The ci- ty shall be flou- ri- shing, her cit- i- zens a- bound In num- ber shall, like to _ the grass that grows up- on the ground.
w: 16.~His name for ev- er shall en- dure; last like the sun it shall: Men shall be blessed in him, _ and blessed all na- tions shall him call.
w: 17.~Now bless- ed be the Lord our God, the God of Is- ra- el, For he a- lone doth won- _ drous works, in glo- ry that ex- cel.
w: 18.~And bless- ed be his glor- ious name to all e- ter- ni- ty: The whole earth let his glo- _ ry fill. A- men, so let it be.
